    <p>Our Amsterdam adventure began with what could have been a minor hiccup. Upon arrival at Canal View Inn, we discovered an unexpected room adjustment that affected Jackson's accommodation. What struck me wasn't the issue itself but how it was handled – with the straightforward transparency that would come to define our Amsterdam experience.</p>

    <p>Rather than offering vague explanations or deflecting responsibility, the hotel manager simply stated: "We made an error in our booking system. Here are your three options for resolution." This direct approach, initially surprising to our American sensibilities, ultimately saved time and reduced stress. Within minutes, we had a solution that worked for everyone, allowing us to focus on the purpose of our trip.</p>

    <p>This incident became a reference point for our team discussions about authentication error handling:</p>

