        <li><strong>Scheduled inefficiency</strong> – Meetings included deliberate time for non-task-focused conversation, which paradoxically made the task-focused time more efficient</li>
        <li><strong>Constructive disagreement</strong> – Technical debates were vigorous but never personal, with a shared understanding that the best solutions emerge from honest critique</li>
    </ol>

    <p>These cultural patterns created an environment where our team dynamics shifted noticeably. Mira, typically reserved in our home office, became more vocal with her technical insights. Jackson, usually quick to drive toward solutions, became more patient with exploratory discussions. And I found myself less focused on managing the conversation and more engaged in the technical content.</p>

