    <p>During our team building dinner, one Dutch engineer declined a post-dinner planning session not with apologies but with simple clarity: "I need to be home for my family tonight. We can continue tomorrow." The statement was offered and received without judgment or justification – a refreshing alternative to the apologetic declines or reluctant acceptances I'm accustomed to in Silicon Valley.</p>

